// core/blocks/template/hypothesis.en.md
var hypothesis_en_default = '## Claim\nOne statement that can be refuted, with the subject, the conditions and the direction stated. No reasons or evidence here.\n\n## Current judgment\nKeep only one: untested, leaning support, leaning against or refuted, with a short reason and what is missing. No weak/medium/strong rating (the Strength label has it). This takes precedence over the earlier rule for inconsistencies: list one only; on change rewrite it, log "from X to Y: reason".\n\n## If true we would see\nConcrete predictions that can be checked, one per line.\n\n## What would refute it\nCounter-conditions written in advance: which result would mean the claim fails.\n\n## How to test\nWhat data to look for, and what comparison or experiment to run.\n\n## Evidence table\nA four-column Markdown table whose header row is written exactly as `| Evidence | Supports or refutes | Strength | Linked topic |`, one row per piece of evidence, each with its source. Write linked topics only here, as topic links; do not restate the supporting and refuting content elsewhere.\n\n## Sources\nOnly the source list, which is added to the end of this section automatically; do not restate the body.\n\n## Update log\nAdd only one line saying what this update changed.\n';

